{
  "skip": false,
  "summary": "Adds BlockedEmail (with match-count/last-match stats), extracts email validation into EmailValidator, and makes the signup form remember rejected emails client-side. The BlockedEmail model and validator logic are reasonable and tested, but the new stats-mutation has a double-counting bug caused by how the controller already validates the user twice per request.",
  "event": "REQUEST_CHANGES",
  "findings": [
    {
      "path": "lib/validators/email_validator.rb",
      "line": 13,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "severity": "Important",
      "title": "BlockedEmail stats double-counted per signup request",
      "body": "`BlockedEmail.should_block?` mutates and saves `match_count`/`last_match_at` as a side effect of validation. `UsersController#create` (app/controllers/users_controller.rb:168) calls `user.valid?` explicitly and then calls `user.save`, which re-runs validations internally — so for a single signup attempt against a blocked email, this validator runs twice and `match_count` is incremented twice, corrupting the very stats this feature exists to track.",
      "suggestion": null
    }
  ]
}

